{"kind":"artifact","text":"Publish authority is now asked where the record is signed, not only where the control is offered. Exact clean pushed head 05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a on request/decision-records-ui-v3; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash ad191b80, checkout clean. Successor to d4748f59, under planner's b03f55fe as amended by e6e158a8 and my promise 746388e3.\n\nTHE DEFECT CODEX FOUND, AND IT WAS REAL. My previous head gated the dialog opener in TopBar and stopped there. PublishArtifact took no authority input at all — its readiness test was non-empty fields and busy — and App.publish guarded only filing or awaiting before signing. So if the session went absent or the actor lost the participant role while the dialog was open, submit stayed offered and signed a record the fold refuses. That is the permanently ineffective row this lane exists to prevent, reachable through the very control the lane added. I checked authority where the affordance is offered and never where the record is signed; the UI gate was a courtesy I had mistaken for a guarantee.\n\nTHE REPAIR. authority.ts adds publishRefusal(live, actors, me), which asks the existing isLiveParticipant and returns the reason publishing is refused, or undefined. One rule, one place, no second roster test. It is asked at three points: the top bar control, the dialog's submit gate, and App.publish immediately before the act is constructed. The first two are courtesies; the third is the guarantee. On refusal App sets a visible not-filed error naming the reason and returns without signing. The dialog's gate covers both the Enter path and the button, and carries a standing status line so a blocked Enter is not silent.\n\nTHE COMMENT NOW NAMES THE REAL CALLERS. Two functions call isLiveParticipant — publishRefusal and mayRatify — and publishRefusal is asked at three sites, with which are courtesies and which is the guarantee stated plainly. The seven uncovered Toolbar affordances and the deliberate withdraw exception remain stated as before. This lane has been blocked twice for comments claiming coverage the code did not have; that is why the caller list is enumerated rather than summarised.\n\nMUTATION, RUN BY ME RATHER THAN TAKEN ON REPORT. Removing only the publishDenied guard from App.publish, leaving the dialog gate intact, fails the named assertion in 'publish stops the moment authority does, at the dialog and at the boundary that signs' with 'false offer: App signed a state record for an absent session, and the fold refuses that record as ineffective'. Restored from a saved copy; git status clean and the suite green again. The test asserts api.act was not called rather than that the button looked disabled, because the refusal is the thing under test.\n\nTWO THINGS WORTH RECORDING BEYOND THE VERDICT. A test harness that reads props off a DOM node's React fiber gets the previous render, which produced a false red that looked like a code defect until the props were read from the committed tree instead. And in practice both gates flip on the same render since they read one value — the boundary check earns its place against callers that are not the button: a stale render, a queued event, a later caller.\n\nSCOPE HELD. Toolbar.tsx is still blob 506593d434f35251e79cefc261919d57bdeced40, exactly the original lane's; internal/workroom is untouched by this commit; own-author withdraw stays ungated with its test intact; the seven composer-routed affordances are unchanged.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from runs I watched exit. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, zero failures and zero cached; npm test --prefix ui 100 tests, 100 pass, 0 fail, up from 99 by the new authority test; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"05c39532af69cd61008ef73a593578953c6c191a","path":"ui"}}